{
  "bridge_text": "那棵大树在寒风中低语，仿佛在等着莉娜的到来。我们就从莉娜站在那棵发出嗡嗡声的大树旁继续讲起吧。",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "莉娜屏住呼吸，伸出手轻轻触摸粗糙的树干，那股奇特的嗡嗡声顺着指尖钻进了她的心里。她鼓起勇气，钻进了树干上那道黑漆漆的缝隙，发现里面藏着一圈盘旋向下的楼梯。在最顶层的台阶上，坐着一只穿着补丁绿背心的老灰狐，他正用那双如干树叶般的眼睛注视着她。"
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s1"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The secret of his grumpiness hides in the shadows of the tree, waiting for the right moment to be told. Let us follow the fox as he begins his journey down the stairs.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Lina stood her ground, her eyes bright with curiosity. Mosk’s ears twitched at her reply, his gaze softening just a fraction. He looked at the girl, then at the dark, winding path below, realizing that she was not going to leave until the mystery of the humming was solved."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With Mosk’s name tucked safely in our memories, Lina stood firm on that dusty wooden step, her eyes fixed on the fox who guarded the secrets of the hollow tree.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed toward the exit, his gaze stern. Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season, setting it gently on the step between them as a token of kindness. She told him it was for the trouble of walking her down. Mosk stared at the fruit for a long time, his expression softening, until he finally stood up, adjusted his green vest, and led the way down the stairs."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Deep at the bottom, the humming transformed into a quiet, mournful song. A firefly the size of a robin lay upon a bed of moss, her luminous glow flickering and fading. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked at her. He whispered that she had been his friend once, but long ago, he had failed to bring her the medicine she needed. Ever since that winter, he had kept watch over the tree, too ashamed to face her."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "While Lina believes a kind heart opens more doors than a thief's path, Mosk still watches the gift with heavy, thoughtful eyes. He finally turns toward the stairs, ready to show her what lies beneath.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his gaze lingering on the bright skin. Then he stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word. The wood groaned softly under his weight, echoing into the hollow depths below as they began their descent into the shadows."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Just like that soft, velvet bed of moss kept the firefly warm, the quiet air in the tree seemed to hold its breath for what would happen next.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming drifted like a quiet song. A firefly the size of a robin lay resting on a bed of moss, which felt as soft and cushioned as a velvet blanket. Her glow was fading, dimming with every flicker. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked at her. He whispered that she had once been his dear friend, but one winter long ago, he had failed to bring her the medicine she needed. Ever since that day, he had guarded the hollow tree, too ashamed to look her in the eye."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With that old fox watching her closely from the top step, Lina stood her ground, waiting to see what he would do next in the quiet hollow.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, Lina discovered a narrow curl of stairs winding downward. Perched upon the very top step sat an old, grey fox wearing a worn, patched green vest. His name was Mosk. In a voice as thin and raspy as dry, rustling autumn leaves, he warned her that this tree was no place for visitors and she ought to return home and forget the mysterious humming. Lina shook her head, insisting she could never forget a song she had yet to hear."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The apple sat heavy and bright on the wooden step, a small offering in the dim light of the hollow tree. Mosk finally turned his gaze away from the fruit and began his slow, rhythmic descent down the winding stairs.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
