      "text": "Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his ancient eyes reflecting its crimson skin. Then he stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word. The wood groaned under his weight, echoing into the shadows below as they began their descent into the heart of the tree."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The firefly's light flickers softly as we wait to see if she can find her strength again. Let us see what happens when Lina reaches out to help.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "The firefly's glow remained dim, casting long shadows against the wooden walls. Mosk's whiskers trembled as he remembered that cold winter long ago, and he stood very still, hoping that perhaps this time, the story would have a different ending."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt and asked the firefly queen what she needed. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, said the queen, that was all medicine ever was. Mosk fetched the milk in a thimble and laid his paw beside hers. The queen's glow steadied. The humming inside the tree turned into a tune Lina had not heard before — and Mosk, for the first time in years, hummed along."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
