{
  "bridge_text": "With the apple left behind on the step, the grumpy fox began his descent. The path downward grew quiet, leading them to a secret waiting in the shadows.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming deepened into a soft, rhythmic song. A firefly, large as a robin, lay motionless upon a bed of emerald moss, her once-bright glow flickering like a dying ember. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked down at her. He whispered that she had been his companion long ago, but he had failed to bring her aid during a harsh winter, and he had guarded this hollow tree ever since, burdened by his heavy shame."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt beside the cooling light and asked what the queen required to mend her spirit. Only a drop of warm milk and a kind word, the queen murmured, for that is all true medicine ever was. Mosk carefully fetched the milk in a silver thimble, laying his paw gently beside her own. As the queen’s glow steadied and brightened, the humming within the tree transformed into a melody Lina had never heard before, and Mosk finally hummed along, his long solitude fading."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
